Package: attitudedyn
Title: Dynamic Discrete Choice Models for Ordinal Panel Attitudes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Gabriel", "Mihalache", email = "mihalache@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Gabriel Mihalache [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Gabriel Mihalache <mihalache@gmail.com>
Description: Estimates the dynamic ordered-probit model of Nepaul and Stern
    (2026, Political Analysis) for several ordinal attitudes observed in an
    unbalanced panel. The likelihood is a Geweke-Hajivassiliou-Keane
    simulated likelihood with antithetic draws. A dependency-free C++ core
    evaluates the likelihood and its analytic gradient; the R interface is a
    thin wrapper. The latent attitude carries forward from wave to wave, as
    in the authors' Fortran replication program.
